 I wouldn't be surprised if many (non-extropian) people would choose
this, but if there remain any intelligent life-forms which do not
choose this limitation (either by retaining biological form or by
evolving artificially), the life-forms without the permanently
stabilized nervous system would soon become increasingly more powerful.
Since this implies trusting your continued existence to life-forms who
may eventually think of you the way a human thinks of a bacterium, It
is not obvious that this approach produces immortality.

>  2)   Capture the development process at a young age (allow the
